failure_location.quote:
Let \(\bar u\in C\bigl([0,T];L^{2}(\Omega)\bigr)\cap L^{2}\bigl(0,T;H^{1}(\Omega)\bigr)\) be the weak solution of  
		\begin{align*}
			\partial_{t}\bar u-\Delta\bar u+v(\bar u)&=f_{\bar\theta} \mathbf 1_{\omega} \quad\text{in }Q_{T},\\
			\bar u&=0 \quad\text{on }\Sigma_{T},\\
			\bar u(T)&=z_{0} \quad\text{in }\Omega .
		\end{align*}

diagnostic_evidence.quote:
The controllability estimate of \cite[Theorem 4.1]{zuazua2024exactcontrollabilitystabilizationwave} yields a constant \(C_3 = C_3 (Q_{T},\mathcal L_{v})\) such that
		\begin{align}\label{eq:f_est2}
			\|f-f_{\bar{\theta}}\|_{L^2(q_T)}
			&\le C_3  (\|u_0-\bar{u}(0)\|_{H^1(\Omega)}+\|u_1-\partial_t \bar{u}(0)\|_{L^2(\Omega)})\\
			&\le C_3  (\|u_0-u_{\theta}(0)\|_{H^1(\Omega)}+\|u_1-\partial_t u_{\theta}(0)\|_{L^2(\Omega)}+\|\hat{u}(0)\|_{H^1(\Omega)}+\|\partial_t \hat{u}(0)\|_{L^2(\Omega)})\nonumber.
		\end{align}

